%% DM26-0670

%% A secret in a signed document, the author's side and the first arrival, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/signed-configuration.md, "Secrets in a document").
%% All of a credential's life, with the protocol handler that hands it over and uses it and what a restart does, is general/escrowed_credential_lifecycle.
sequenceDiagram
    actor Author
    participant Sign as polar-sign
    participant Front as Credentials observer<br/>(its gateway)
    participant CredAgent as Credentials agent
    participant Repo as Repo and scheduler
    participant Config as Target's ConfigurationActor
    participant Handler as Target's handler
    participant Crypto as Target's CryptoActor

    autonumber
    Note over Author,Front: The agent's scaffold marks secret fields, so the tool knows which to encrypt
    Author->>Sign: sign the section for agent X, the secret typed or on standard input
    Sign->>Front: POST /agent-escrow-key { identity }, no authentication
    Front->>CredAgent: AgentEscrowKeyRequest
    CredAgent-->>Front: the escrow certificate, which is public
    Front-->>Sign: the escrow certificate of agent X
    Sign->>Sign: it chains to the author's CA, is valid now, may be sealed to, and names X:<br/>a swapped key on the way back fails here
    Sign->>Sign: encrypt each secret field to that key, bound to agent, section, version, entry and field
    Sign->>Sign: sign: the signature covers the ciphertext
    Sign-->>Author: the plaintext is never written to the file
    Author->>Repo: push, then delivery as in the delivery diagram

    Repo-)Config: document for agent X
    Config->>Config: verify the signature and every other check first, and judge<br/>the section's shape, opening nothing
    Config-)Handler: RuntimeChanged
    Handler->>Crypto: RegisterSecret for each entry, with its binding<br/>(the hosts it may be used for)
    Crypto-->>Handler: registered (the custody daemon unwraps,<br/>and the private key never leaves it)
    Handler->>Crypto: ReplaceSection: drop what this version leaves out

    Note over Crypto,CredAgent: Closing the loop, in the background, retried until acknowledged
    Crypto->>CredAgent: EscrowKeyRequest, then StoreSecret
    CredAgent-->>Crypto: stored

    Note over Handler,Crypto: Later, whenever a request needs it, only the protocol<br/>handler can ask, and it gets what that protocol presents,<br/>for a host the binding allows (UseCredential)
